\cf3 > \cf4 "Phase 5: Resumable Chunked Video Upload System.\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 Context: PHP limits prevent uploading large course videos (e.g., 1GB). We need a chunked upload strategy.\cf2 \
  \cf4 Action Required:\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 1. CONTROLLER ('app/Controllers/UploadController.php'):\cf2 \
  \cf4    - Method 'uploadChunk()':\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Accept POST params: file_data, file_name, chunk_index, total_chunks.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Store chunks in 'storage/temp/\{session_id\}/'.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * If it's the LAST chunk:\cf2 \
  \cf4        - Merge all chunks into a single file in 'public/uploads/videos/'.\cf2 \
  \cf4        - Delete temp chunks.\cf2 \
  \cf4        - Return JSON: \{ status: 'success', file_path: '/uploads/videos/...' \}.\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 2. ROUTE ('routes/web.php'):\cf2 \
  \cf4    - POST '/upload/chunk' -> [UploadController::class, 'uploadChunk'].\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 3. FRONTEND LOGIC (Create a reusable JS file 'public/assets/js/uploader.js'):\cf2 \
  \cf4    - Create a class/function 'ChunkedUploader'.\cf2 \
  \cf4    - Logic:\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Take a file input.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Slice file into 2MB chunks using File.prototype.slice.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Loop and send POST requests sequentially.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Update a progress bar (UI).\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Handle retries on failure.\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 4. INTEGRATION:\cf2 \
  \cf4    - Update 'resources/views/instructor/course_builder.php':\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Replace the simple file input with this new Uploader component.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * Show a Progress Bar during upload.\cf2 \
  \cf4      * When complete, put the returned URL into a hidden input field for the Lesson.\cf2 \
\
  \cf4 Provide the full code for UploadController and the JavaScript uploader logic."\cf2 \
