\f1\b Phase 8: Student Quiz Runner
\f0\b0 , I plan to build the actual exam interface where students take the quiz. Here is the roadmap:\
\
  
\f1\b 1. View: \cf3 resources/views/learn/quiz_runner.php
\f0\b0 \cf2 \
  This will be a focused, distraction-free environment (similar to the Video Player but specialized for testing).\
   * 
\f1\b UI Layout
\f0\b0 :\
       * 
\f1\b Header
\f0\b0 : Timer (Countdown), Current Question Index (e.g., "Question 5 of 10"), and "Exit" button.\
       * 
\f1\b Main Card
\f0\b0 : The Question itself (Text/Media) + Answer Options (Radios/Checkboxes).\
       * 
\f1\b Navigation
\f0\b0 : "Previous", "Next" (or "Submit" on last question).\
       * 
\f1\b Sidebar (Optional)
\f0\b0 : Question navigator grid (dots) to jump between questions.\
\
  
\f1\b 2. Controller: \cf3 QuizRunnerController
\f0\b0 \cf2 \
   * \cf3 start($quizId)\cf2 : Initializes an attempt record in \cf3 quiz_attempts\cf2  (sets \cf3 started_at\cf2 ).\
   * \cf3 show($attemptId)\cf2 : Renders the Quiz Runner view. Loads questions (shuffled if randomization is on).\
   * \cf3 submitAnswer($attemptId)\cf2 : AJAX endpoint to save an answer for a specific question (auto-save logic).\
   * \cf3 finish($attemptId)\cf2 : Grades the quiz, calculates score, updates \cf3 is_passed\cf2 , and redirects to the 
\f1\b Results Page
\f0\b0 .\
\
  
\f1\b 3. View: \cf3 resources/views/learn/quiz_results.php
\f0\b0 \cf2 \
   * Displays the final score (e.g., "85%").\
   * Pass/Fail Badge.\
   * 
\f1\b Feedback Section
\f0\b0 : If enabled by the instructor, shows a breakdown of questions, the user's answer, the correct answer, and the\
     explanation.\
   * "Retake Quiz" button (if attempts allow) or "Continue Course".\
\
  
\f1\b 4. JavaScript Logic (\cf3 public/assets/js/quiz_runner.js\cf2 )
\f0\b0 \
   * 
\f1\b Timer
\f0\b0 : Handles the countdown and auto-submits when time runs out.\
   * 
\f1\b State Management
\f0\b0 : Tracks current question index locally to avoid page reloads (SPA feel).\
   * 
\f1\b Auto-Save
\f0\b0 : Sends answers to the backend whenever an option is selected.\
