\f1\b The Issue: \cf3 ON DELETE CASCADE\cf2  is not working.
\f0\b0 \
  Although our migration scripts included \cf3 FOREIGN KEY ... ON DELETE CASCADE\cf2 , SQLite 
\f1\b does not enforce Foreign Key constraints by default
\f0\b0 .\
  You must explicitly enable them for 
\f2\i every
\f0\i0  connection using \cf3 PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\cf2 .\
\
  While our migration scripts ran \cf3 PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\cf2 , the \cf3 App\\Core\\Database\cf2  class connection (used by the Controllers and this test\
  script) does 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  seem to enable this setting automatically upon connecting.\
\
  This means if an instructor deletes a Course or Module, the child content (Lessons, Quizzes, Questions) becomes 
\f1\b orphaned
\f0\b0  (junk data)\
  instead of being deleted.\
\
  
