\cf3 \uc0\u10022  \cf2 I have implemented the Resumable Chunked Video Upload System.\
\
  
\f1\b Summary of Changes:
\f0\b0 \
   1. 
\f1\b Backend (`app/Controllers/UploadController.php`)
\f0\b0 :\
       * Created \cf3 uploadChunk\cf2  method to handle sequential chunk uploads.\
       * Implements logic to store temp chunks and merge them into a final video file when complete.\
       * Returns the final file path.\
\
   2. 
\f1\b Frontend Logic (`public/assets/js/uploader.js`)
\f0\b0 :\
       * Created \cf3 ChunkedUploader\cf2  class to slice files and manage upload state.\
       * Includes progress tracking and retry logic.\
       * Exposes \cf3 window.initChunkedUploader\cf2  helper.\
\
   3. 
\f1\b UI Integration (`resources/views/instructor/course_builder.php`)
\f0\b0 :\
       * Replaced the simple URL input with a dynamic file uploader.\
       * Added a progress bar.\
       * Uses Alpine.js \cf3 x-data\cf2  to manage unique IDs per module (\cf3 module_id\cf2 ) and toggle between Video Upload and URL Input.\
       * Includes an inline script to initialize the uploader when a user interacts with the file input.\
\
   4. 
\f1\b Routes (`routes/web.php`)
\f0\b0 :\
       * Added \cf3 POST /upload/chunk\cf2  route.\
\
   5. 
\f1\b Layout
\f0\b0 : Restored FontAwesome for icons.\
\
  
\f1\b How to Test:
\f0\b0 \
   1. Go to the Course Builder (\cf3 /instructor/course/\{id\}/edit\cf2 ).\
   2. Add a new Module.\
   3. Click "+ Add Lesson".\
   4. Select "Video" type. You should see the file input.\
   5. Select a large video file (e.g., > 10MB).\
   6. Watch the progress bar.\
   7. Once complete, the progress bar turns green, and the hidden input is populated with the local path (e.g., \cf3 /uploads/videos/xxxx.mp4\cf2 ).\
   8. Click the submit button (Checkmark icon) to save the lesson.\
\
