   2. 
\f1\b Controller
\f0\b0 : \cf3 App\\Controllers\\LearnController\cf2  is ready.\
       * \cf3 show()\cf2 : Fetches the course playlist and renders the player. It handles "Prev/Next" logic.\
       * \cf3 trackProgress()\cf2 : Records xAPI statements (started, watched_50, completed) and updates course completion status.\
   3. 
\f1\b View
\f0\b0 : \cf3 resources/views/learn/player.php\cf2  created.\
       * 
\f1\b Dark Immersive Mode
\f0\b0 : Uses \cf3 zinc-950\cf2  background.\
       * 
\f1\b Playlist Sidebar
\f0\b0 : Shows lesson progress with checkmarks.\
       * 
\f1\b Video Player
\f0\b0 : HTML5 video with controls.\
   4. 
\f1\b JavaScript
\f0\b0 : \cf3 public/assets/js/player.js\cf2  tracks video events (\cf3 play\cf2 , \cf3 timeupdate\cf2 , \cf3 ended\cf2 ) and sends AJAX requests to the backend. It also shows a "Lesson Completed" toast\
      notification.\
   5. 
\f1\b Routes
\f0\b0 : Added regex-based route for \cf3 /learn/\{course_id\}/lesson/\{lesson_id\}\cf2  to handle dynamic IDs.\
\
  
\f1\b How to Test:
\f0\b0 \
   1. 
\f1\b Create Content
\f0\b0 : Use the Instructor Builder to create a course with a video lesson.\
   2. 
\f1\b Access Player
\f0\b0 : Since we haven't built a "Enroll" button yet, manually navigate to:\
      \cf3 /learn/\{course_id\}/lesson/\{lesson_id\}\cf2  (Replace IDs with actual numbers, e.g., \cf3 /learn/1/lesson/1\cf2 ).\
   3. 
\f1\b Watch Video
\f0\b0 : Play the video. Open your browser console to see "Tracked: started".\
   4. 
\f1\b Finish Video
\f0\b0 : Seek to the end. The "Lesson Completed" toast will appear, and the sidebar icon for that lesson will turn into a green checkmark (on page refresh).\
