\cf3 \uc0\u10022  \cf2 If the "Add Question" button is 
\f2\i still
\f0\i0  doing nothing (no page reload, no network request), it is almost certainly a client-side validation issue preventing the form submission. The\
  browser is likely trying to tell you a field is invalid, but the message is hidden or the field is off-screen.\
\
  
\f1\b Suspect: Hidden Required Fields
\f0\b0 \
  In the \cf3 quiz_builder.php\cf2  view, we have:\
\
   \cf4 1 <\cf8 input\cf4  \cf6 type\cf4 =\cf7 "text"\cf4  \cf6 name\cf4 =\cf7 "option_text[]"\cf4  \cf6 required\cf4  \cf6 ...\cf4 >\cf2 \
  These inputs are inside a \cf3 template\cf2  loop. However, we also have logic that shows/hides the entire "Answer Options" block based on \cf3 type\cf2 .\
\
  
\f1\b Scenario:
\f0\b0 \
   1. You select "True / False".\
   2. The "Answer Options" (text inputs) are hidden via \cf3 x-show\cf2 .\
   3. However, if those inputs still exist in the DOM (just hidden with CSS \cf3 display: none\cf2 ), and they have the \cf3 required\cf2  attribute, the browser will try to validate them. Since they are\
      empty and hidden, the form submit fails silently (or with a console error "An invalid form control with name='...' is not focusable.").\
\
  
\f1\b Wait, `x-show` just adds `display: none`. It does NOT remove elements from the DOM.
\f0\b0 \
  So if \cf3 type === 'true_false'\cf2 , the text inputs for Single/Multi choice are hidden BUT still \cf3 required\cf2 . The browser blocks submission because they are empty.\
\
  
\f1\b Fix:
\f0\b0 \
  We need to ensure \cf3 required\cf2  is only applied when the input is visible. We can use Alpine's \cf3 :required="type !== 'true_false'"\cf2  binding.\
\
  Also, \cf3 x-if\cf2  is better than \cf3 x-show\cf2  for this as it physically adds/removes elements from the DOM, but \cf3 x-if\cf2  requires a \cf3 <template>\cf2  tag root.\
\
  
\f1\b Simpler Fix:
\f0\b0  Update the input attributes to toggle \cf3 required\cf2  and \cf3 disabled\cf2 . If disabled, they won't block submission and won't send data.\
\
  I will modify \cf3 quiz_builder.php\cf2  to disable the option inputs when \cf3 type === 'true_false'\cf2 .\
\
  Similarly, for the True/False radios, they are always present? No, they are in a \cf3 div\cf2  with \cf3 x-show\cf2 . We need to handle them too.\
\
