\cf3 > \cf4 How is "Hours Learned" working in Dashboard ?\cf2 \
\
\cf3 \uc0\u10022  \cf2 The 
\f1\b "Hours Learned"
\f0\b0  metric on the Dashboard is calculated dynamically based on the 
\f1\b duration of completed video lessons
\f0\b0 .\
\
  
\f1\b How it Works (Under the Hood):
\f0\b0 \
\
   1. 
\f1\b Data Source
\f0\b0 : It queries the \cf3 completed_lessons\cf2  table to find all lesson IDs that the user has finished.\
   2. 
\f1\b Aggregation
\f0\b0 : It joins this list with the \cf3 lessons\cf2  table.\
   3. 
\f1\b Calculation
\f0\b0 : It sums up the \cf3 duration\cf2  column (which stores the length of videos in seconds) for all those completed lessons.\
   4. 
\f1\b Conversion
\f0\b0 : It divides the total seconds by 3600 to get the total 
\f1\b Hours
\f0\b0 , rounded down (\cf3 floor\cf2 ).\
\
  
\f1\b The SQL Query Used:
\f0\b0 \
\
   \cf4 1 \cf8 SELECT\cf2  \cf9 SUM\cf2 (l.duration) \cf8 as\cf2  seconds\
   \cf4 2 \cf8 FROM\cf2  completed_lessons cl\
   \cf4 3 \cf8 JOIN\cf2  lessons l \cf8 ON\cf2  cl.lesson_id = l.id\
   \cf4 4 \cf8 WHERE\cf2  cl.user_id = :uid\
\
  
\f1\b Potential Limitation:
\f0\b0 \
  Currently, the \cf3 duration\cf2  column in \cf3 lessons\cf2  might be 
\f1\b NULL
\f0\b0  or 
\f1\b 0
\f0\b0  for many lessons because:\
   1. 
\f1\b Video Uploads
\f0\b0 : The current uploader saves the file but 
\f1\b does not
\f0\b0  automatically extract metadata (like duration) from the video file (this usually requires \cf3 FFmpeg\cf2  installed on the\
      server).\
   2. 
\f1\b Quizzes/Articles
\f0\b0 : These types often don't have a "duration" set.\
\
  
\f1\b Result:
\f0\b0 \
  If your video lessons have a \cf3 duration\cf2  of \cf3 0\cf2  or \cf3 NULL\cf2  in the database, the "Hours Learned" will essentially stay at 
\f1\b 0h
\f0\b0  regardless of how many lessons you complete.\
\
  
\f1\b Recommendation for Improvement:
\f0\b0 \
  To make this metric real, we have two options:\
   1. 
\f1\b Manual Input
\f0\b0 : Add a "Duration (minutes)" field to the "Add Lesson" form so instructors can manually specify how long a lesson is (video or reading time).\
   2. 
\f1\b Auto-Detection
\f0\b0 : Integrate \cf3 php-ffmpeg\cf2  to read the duration during upload (Requires server binaries).\
\
  
\f1\b Option 1 (Manual Input)
\f0\b0  is the most robust and easiest to implement immediately without external dependencies. Would you like me to add a "Duration" field to the Course Builder?\
\
