\cf3 > \cf4 Why doesn't it appear on the homepage that I logged in?\cf2 \
\
\cf3 \uc0\u10022 \cf2  The issue is likely that the \cf3 HomeController\cf2  is checking \cf3 isset($_SESSION['user_id'])\cf2 , but the session might not be started properly when hitting the landing page, or the caching of\
  the view is interfering.\
\
  
\f1\b Root Cause Analysis:
\f0\b0 \
  In \cf3 public/index.php\cf2 , we do:\
\
   \cf4 1 \cf8 if\cf2  (file_exists(BASE_PATH . \cf7 '.env'\cf2 )) \{ ... \}\
   \cf4 2 // Initialize Router\cf2 \
   \cf4 3 // Load Routes\cf2 \
   \cf4 4 // Dispatch\cf2 \
  We 
\f1\b do NOT
\f0\b0  call \cf3 session_start()\cf2  globally in \cf3 index.php\cf2 .\
  Instead, individual Controllers/Middleware call it.\
\
  The \cf3 HomeController\cf2  currently looks like this:\
\
   \cf4 1 \cf8 public\cf2  \cf8 function\cf2  index(): void\
   \cf4 2 \cf2 \{\
   \cf4 3 \cf2     \cf3 $isLoggedIn\cf2  = \cf8 isset\cf2 (\cf3 $_SESSION\cf2 [\cf7 'user_id'\cf2 ]);\
   \cf4 4 \cf2     \cf3 $this\cf2 ->view(\cf7 'home'\cf2 , [\cf7 'isLoggedIn'\cf2  => \cf3 $isLoggedIn\cf2 ]);\
   \cf4 5 \cf2 \}\
  
\f1\b The Problem:
\f0\b0  \cf3 session_start()\cf2  is never called in \cf3 HomeController\cf2 . So \cf3 $_SESSION\cf2  is undefined or empty, even if a cookie exists.\
\
  
\f1\b Fix:
\f0\b0 \
  I must add \cf3 session_start()\cf2  to the \cf3 HomeController\cf2  (or better, check the status before accessing \cf3 $_SESSION\cf2 ).\
\
