\cf3 > \cf4 If I wanna need to use specaific images where I need to add it in the folder?\cf2 \
\
\cf3 \uc0\u10022  \cf2 For a professional structure, all images should be placed inside the \cf3 public/\cf2  directory, as this is the only folder accessible by the web browser.\
\
  Here is the recommended organization:\
\
  
\f1\b 1. Static UI Images (Logos, Backgrounds, Icons)
\f0\b0 \
  Place these in:\
  \cf3 public/assets/images/\cf2 \
\
  
\f1\b Example:
\f0\b0 \
   * \cf3 public/assets/images/logo.png\cf2 \
   * \cf3 public/assets/images/hero-bg.jpg\cf2 \
\
  
\f1\b How to use them in your code:
\f0\b0 \
\
   \cf4 1 <\cf8 img\cf4  \cf6 src\cf4 =\cf7 "/assets/images/logo.png"\cf4  \cf6 alt\cf4 =\cf7 "Scratch LMS Logo"\cf4 >\cf2 \
\
  \cf14 ---\cf2 \
\
  
\f1\b 2. Course-Related Content (Dynamic Uploads)
\f0\b0 \
  Place these in:\
  \cf3 public/uploads/\cf2 \
\
  
\f2\i Note: We already configured the Course Builder to save thumbnails to `public/uploads/` and videos to `public/uploads/videos/`.
\f0\i0 \
\
  \cf14 ---\cf2 \
\
  
